BUGFIX: catalog children listed grouped controls at the catalog level too, so controls appeared twice (once under the catalog, once under their group) in tree/graph. Cause: GORM Preload("Controls") on a Catalog returns EVERY control by catalog_id (grouped ones included), so catalogTopControls wrongly held group members. Fix in loadCatalogs: build the group-membership set first, then catalogTopControls = catalog controls NOT in any group; catalogAllControls now dedups (group controls + only-ungrouped controls). Verified on live data (catalog f47..401: was 8 groups + ~10 duplicated controls -> now 8 groups, 0 top-level controls, no overlap with group children). Added integration test TestLineageGrouping.
